  <data name="Settings_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Settings</value>
    <comment>Settings window title, and the heading at the top of it.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Language" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Language</value>
    <comment>Label beside the language dropdown.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Language_System" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>System</value>
    <comment>Language dropdown row meaning "follow the operating system's language". The other rows are language names, which are never translated.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_LaunchAtLogin" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Launch at login</value>
    <comment>Checkbox: start the app when the user signs in to Windows.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_CheckForUpdates" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Check for updates on launch</value>
    <comment>Checkbox: look for a newer release at startup.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_AutoDownloadAssets" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Automatically download device images</value>
    <comment>Checkbox: fetch product photos for the device gallery.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_MinimizeToTray" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Minimize to the system tray (hide from the taskbar)</value>
    <comment>Checkbox. "System tray" is the Windows notification area.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_SuppressLogging" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Suppress diagnostic logs</value>
    <comment>Checkbox: stop writing the diagnostic log file.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Footer" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Settings are saved to config.toml. Update checks are enabled by default.</value>
    <comment>Grey footnote under the settings list. "config.toml" is a filename - do not translate it.</comment>
